  "body": "# Getting the Cert\r\n\r\nI get my cert with certbot -> save it to /etc/letsencrypt. It gets the 0640 treatment and ```chown root:ssl-cert``` with a post-hook.\r\n\r\nCreate symlink to /etc/ssl/certs and /etc/ssl/private (644 and 640) respectivaly.\r\n\r\nI mount them to /etc/ssl/cert and /etc/ssl/private inside the synapse docker container.\r\n\r\nI create a matrix user to /opt/matrix (home dir). I launch the Docker container per instructions with $UID and $GID pointing to host machine matrix user so when i mount /opt/matrix/synapse to /data it has the same permissions to RW. \r\n\r\nNow when I launch the container it cant read the /etc/ssl/private/key.pem when I specify it under the homeserver.yaml (permission denied)\r\n\r\nWhen I launch the docker container and go inside the container I can see it with root, ofcousre. But then I find out that /etc/passwd and /etc/group does not contain the UID and GID I have created and launched the docker container with. \r\n\r\nHow can I make the privatekey readable without 0644?",
